# Wallet P2P + messagebox

Full plan: [`docs/wallet-p2p-messagebox.md`](../../docs/wallet-p2p-messagebox.md).

## Vocabulary

- **P2P** = counterparty gets value/facts without an indexer deciding ownership/identity.
  - **A** chain custody (P2PKH tip)
  - **B** identity messagebox (BRC-33; any host)
  - **C** convenience (GorillaPool content, handle resolve)
- **BRC-150 remittance** (`customInstructions.provenance`) is **local** — does not travel on P2PKH. It is the **only** item authenticity/identity model; **BRC-156 (soft-latch) was cancelled and fully removed** — there is no on-chain latch companion.
- Item tips are plain P2PKH; item identity/authenticity is the BRC-150 offline tip→origin proof, not on-chain state.
- **Messagebox** = BRC-33 store-and-forward. **BRC-CLOUD is a convenience host**, not required for custody. Prefer resolved `messagebox` URL from handle resolve; do not hardcode our cloud as the only box forever. A live pair may upgrade to a signed IPv6 socket (draft BRC-246, `directSession/`). The box stays the rendezvous and the offline inbox. Never put the endpoint in a handle record.
- Device peer / BRC-39 = same-identity sync, not counterparty P2P.

## When changing send / receive / chat

1. Custody paths stay grade A; never gate collectable/BSV success on messagebox.
2. Do not describe remittance as “sent to the peer.”
3. Chat delivery takes a box base URL (`Friend.messagebox` → `deliverOutbound`); BRC-CLOUD is fallback only. Bodies are BRC-169 §7 / BRC-78 envelopes. A live IPv6 session (draft BRC-246) carries the same sealed chat. Requests use `X-BRC33-*` (`messageboxAuth.ts`); `X-BRC103-*` on BRC-CLOUD only. Full Authrite Peer sessions are still deferred.
4. Settings statecharts + `layers.ts` glossary must stay accurate if behaviour changes.
5. Do not regress BRC-33 field names (`sender`, `messageIds`, `status: success`).
